DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
22368::$$$message_0177_0000_0000$$$::I always wake up in pain.[lr]::
22369::$$$message_0177_0000_0001$$$::It's a journey where I fall from a lightless abyss to the sunlit surface.[lr]::
22370::$$$message_0177_0000_0002$$$::From dark to light, not unlike the loud trip from womb to birth.[lr]::
22371::$$$message_0177_0000_0003$$$::My battered body and withering life are lit aflame, and my mind returns to the bright world of the living.::
22372::$$$message_0177_0001_0000$$$::"[font color=0x000000][block len=9][resetfont]"[lr]::
22373::$$$message_0177_0001_0001$$$::I writhe in agony.[lr]::
22374::$$$message_0177_0001_0002$$$::The instant I revive, my blood flow, skeletal structure, nervous synapses, and organ operations[line len=2]all of my vital functions[line len=2]give birth to pain.::
22375::$$$message_0177_0002_0000$$$::"[font color=0x000000][block len=9][resetfont]"[lr]::
22376::$$$message_0177_0002_0001$$$::I live in order to suffer.[lr]::
22377::$$$message_0177_0002_0002$$$::My burned-out brain gropes around for its destroyed normality, and the pain restarts my functions.[lr]::
22378::$$$message_0177_0002_0003$$$::In other words, the pain in my body allows me to start thinking like a human.::
22379::$$$message_0177_0003_0000$$$::"[font color=0x000000][block len=9][resetfont]"[lr]::
22380::$$$message_0177_0003_0001$$$::There are hundreds of me now, swarming on top of a pallet.[lr]::
22381::$$$message_0177_0003_0002$$$::I no longer have a clear sense of self. Countless indistinguishable mes are melting together.[lr]::
22382::$$$message_0177_0003_0003$$$::There's a commensurate cost to being resurrected from nothing.::
22383::$$$message_0177_0004_0000$$$::That disorder...[lr]::
22384::$$$message_0177_0004_0001$$$::That feeling of nothingness fuses with the torment.[lr]::
22385::$$$message_0177_0004_0002$$$::I no longer have a self.[lr]::
22386::$$$message_0177_0004_0003$$$::Why am I alive again? Why is this happening to me? The answers to those questions are like a distant event.::
22387::$$$message_0177_0005_0000$$$::I lack a sense of self-awareness.[lr]::
22388::$$$message_0177_0005_0001$$$::Neither happiness nor sadness exist in this innocent, eternally fruitless paradise.::
22389::$$$message_0177_0006_0000$$$::                                    But, [wait canskip=0 time=1000]there's just one thing [wait canskip=0 time=500]that hurts.::
22390::$$$message_0177_0007_0000$$$::...I scratch my cheek.[lr]::
22391::$$$message_0177_0007_0001$$$::In this complete, deep pit...[lr]::
22392::$$$message_0177_0007_0002$$$::Why am I still connected to something so beautiful...?::
22393::$$$message_0177_0008_0000$$$::The first day begins anew.[lr]::
22394::$$$message_0177_0008_0001$$$::The woman leaves, and my beautiful Master Bazett is asleep on the sofa.[lr]::
22395::$$$message_0177_0008_0002$$$::She looks dead.[lr]::
22396::$$$message_0177_0008_0003$$$::The cause is clear: [fadein time=100 storage=a03][fadein time=800 storage=iバゼットの隠れ家_内部-(深夜)]the Servant Saber ran her through the heart in front of the church.[lr]::
22397::$$$message_0177_0008_0004$$$::She'll start breathing again soon enough, so there's no need to wake or bury her.[lr]::
22398::$$$message_0177_0008_0005$$$::I just need to protect this place, as her Servant.::
22399::$$$message_0177_0009_0000$$$::"But man, I'm bored. Maybe I should play a prank on her."[lr]::
22400::$$$message_0177_0009_0001$$$::I'm pretty frank with myself where others ignore the intrusive thoughts.[lr]::
22401::$$$message_0177_0009_0002$$$::As a Servant, I put top billing on my own desires. I can't ignore her.[lr]::
22402::$$$message_0177_0009_0003$$$::Normally, I'd assault and devour her without thinking, leaving the room a mess.::
22403::$$$message_0177_0010_0000$$$::Of course, I wouldn't do that to my Master.[lr]::
22404::$$$message_0177_0010_0001$$$::It would be a real hassle if she woke up in the middle of it.[lr]::
22405::$$$message_0177_0010_0002$$$::I'm used to being hated and killed, but crying faces are a turn-off.::
22406::$$$message_0177_0011_0000$$$::Too bad. Gotta find a simpler way to kill the time.[lr]::
22407::$$$message_0177_0011_0001$$$::Click. Click. Click. Click.[lr]::
22408::$$$message_0177_0011_0002$$$::C-click. C-click. C-click.[sestop storage=se600.wav time=400 nowait=1][lr]::
22409::$$$message_0177_0011_0003$$$::I slide the panel in time with the second hand on the clock.[lr]::
22410::$$$message_0177_0011_0004$$$::Immersed in the game, I increase the tempo.::
22411::$$$message_0177_0012_0000$$$::"...ah..."[lr]::
22412::$$$message_0177_0012_0001$$$::I hear her coquettish breathing from the sofa.::
22413::$$$message_0177_0013_0000$$$::Bazett lightly shakes her head and then glares at me like an enemy.::
22414::$$$message_0177_0014_0000$$$::"Hey. You're awake, Master.[lr]::
22415::$$$message_0177_0014_0001$$$::I hope you're not going to tell me again that your memories are foggy."::
22416::$$$message_0177_0015_0000$$$::"...My memory is fine. I know that you're my Servant, I'm a Master, and that this mansion is our hideout.[lr]::
22417::$$$message_0177_0015_0001$$$::I also remember that my memory was unclear when I woke up here before."[lr]::
22418::$$$message_0177_0015_0002$$$::"Good. That will save us some time. [l][say storage=snplg02_anr_0021 name=アンリ]Then, let's get out of here and continue the Holy Grail War."::
22419::$$$message_0177_0016_0000$$$::"...Wait.[lr]::
22420::$$$message_0177_0016_0001$$$::My memories before this place are vague, but I recall what's happened since. We were defeated, killed, by an enemy Master."::
22421::$$$message_0177_0017_0000$$$::"...Well, well. You don't remember the important parts, but you do remember something crazy.[lr]::
22422::$$$message_0177_0017_0001$$$::So what? It's good enough that you're alive [font italic=true]now[font italic=false]. Don't sweat the details."::
22423::$$$message_0177_0018_0000$$$::"It's not good at all. It's illogical. How can I ignore it?[lr]::
22424::$$$message_0177_0018_0001$$$::...Answer me, Servant. We were defeated, so why are we still alive?"[lr]::
22425::$$$message_0177_0018_0002$$$::"Well, we came back to life, obviously. To be precise, we're back at the first night."::
22426::$$$message_0177_0019_0000$$$::Bazett doesn't look surprised.[lr]::
22427::$$$message_0177_0019_0001$$$::She must have been thinking furiously since she woke up.[lr]::
22428::$$$message_0177_0019_0002$$$::Her mental adaptability is anything but ordinary.[lr]::
22429::$$$message_0177_0019_0003$$$::The problem is that she's either unaware or ashamed of that talent.[lr]::
22430::$$$message_0177_0019_0004$$$::It isn't my place to say anything about it, though.::
22431::$$$message_0177_0020_0000$$$::"...Hmph. If that's true, then I have an impressive Servant.[lr]::
22432::$$$message_0177_0020_0001$$$::Raising the dead is a feat of True Magic, like time travel, operation of parallel worlds, or denial of nothingness.[lr]::
22433::$$$message_0177_0020_0002$$$::Do you claim to be a Heroic Spirit with such miraculous power?"[lr]::
22434::$$$message_0177_0020_0003$$$::Why is she looking at me like that?[lr]::
22435::$$$message_0177_0020_0004$$$::It's clearly a look of doubt. Mockery, even.[lr]::
22436::$$$message_0177_0020_0005$$$::Do I look like a guy who would make outrageous claims like that?::
22437::$$$message_0177_0021_0000$$$::"You can just think of what I do as something emulating it.[lr]::
22438::$$$message_0177_0021_0001$$$::You'll come back to life even if you die. You can redo things as long as we have a pact. No matter who beats you, you can start over from here."::
22439::$$$message_0177_0022_0000$$$::"...I don't understand the theory behind it, but you're saying that we can reset...no, that we're in a loop.[lr]::
22440::$$$message_0177_0022_0001$$$::I don't know what Noble Phantasm that is, but you have the ability to revive at night... No, you skip time back to this moment in which we are still alive in this place.[lr]::
22441::$$$message_0177_0022_0002$$$::So we revive back in time."::
22442::$$$message_0177_0023_0000$$$::"It must a Noble Phantasm with the power to interfere or modify destiny. Certainly worthy of a Heroic Spirit.[lr]::
22443::$$$message_0177_0023_0001$$$::I can believe that no matter how weak you seem."[lr]::
22444::$$$message_0177_0023_0002$$$::Which means she didn't believe me before.[lr]::
22445::$$$message_0177_0023_0003$$$::I guess anyone would be fed up with me, after getting slaughtered without anything to show for it.::
22446::$$$message_0177_0024_0000$$$::"That's right. So relax.[lr]::
22447::$$$message_0177_0024_0001$$$::Yeah, night is a good time for getting killed. I can't fight when it isn't nighttime. I just don't feel like it during the day."::
22448::$$$message_0177_0025_0000$$$::"...So you're saying that your time loop can only activate at night.[lr]::
22449::$$$message_0177_0025_0001$$$::Your Noble Phantasm does sound too powerful to not have such a weakness."[lr]::
22450::$$$message_0177_0025_0002$$$::Actually, she's wrong about a lot of that.[lr]::
22451::$$$message_0177_0025_0003$$$::...Whatever. It still works out the same.::
22452::$$$message_0177_0026_0000$$$::"...Very well. We will only act at night.[lr]::
22453::$$$message_0177_0026_0001$$$::I'll sleep here during the day, so control yourself during that time."[lr]::
22454::$$$message_0177_0026_0002$$$::"You got it. You'd better stay inside during the day, too. I'm really weak during daytime. I'll get killed unless my Master protects me."::
22455::$$$message_0177_0027_0000$$$::"...I understand. I feel that our positions should be reversed, but I've begun to grasp your abilities.[lr]::
22456::$$$message_0177_0027_0001$$$::You're of negligible use in combat, but I haven't seen an ability like yours before. I will handle fighting the Holy Grail War, so you just need to back me up with your unique Noble Phantasm."::
22457::$$$message_0177_0028_0000$$$::"Hmm. That's a lifesaver, but aren't you being a little extreme, Master?[lr]::
22458::$$$message_0177_0028_0001$$$::I can fight a little. I can't promise to defeat a Servant, but I can at least buy some ti[line len=2]"::
22459::$$$message_0177_0029_0000$$$::"After it ended that way? I expect nothing from you, at least in combat. You can just stay there and watch."[lr]::
22460::$$$message_0177_0029_0001$$$::"Haah... That's easier for me, but I don't think we'll be able to win that way. It won't be that easy to separate each Servant from their Master, either."::
22461::$$$message_0177_0030_0000$$$::In the end, the Holy Grail War is about defeating other Servants.[lr]::
22462::$$$message_0177_0030_0001$$$::Good luck killing a Master while their Servant's still kicking.[lr]::
22463::$$$message_0177_0030_0002$$$::But a Servant isn't something a human can handle.[lr]::
22464::$$$message_0177_0030_0003$$$::That's why I'm offering to help, even if I'm not really feeling up to it.[lr]::
22465::$$$message_0177_0030_0004$$$::And yet...::
22466::$$$message_0177_0031_0000$$$::"There's no need to separate them.[lr]::
22467::$$$message_0177_0031_0001$$$::I will defeat the Servants."[lr]::
22468::$$$message_0177_0031_0002$$$::Bazett declares with unshakable confidence.::
22469::$$$message_0177_0032_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
22470::$$$message_0177_0032_0001$$$::...Well, damn.[lr]::
22471::$$$message_0177_0032_0002$$$::I like to think of myself as unflappable most of the time, but that sent a chill up my spine.::
22472::$$$message_0177_0033_0000$$$::"More importantly, I have questions for you.[lr]::
22473::$$$message_0177_0033_0001$$$::You said that you can revive us as many times as needed at night, but what is the price?[lr]::
22474::$$$message_0177_0033_0002$$$::For example, does it consume my Magic Circuits? Is there a limit on the number of times you can use your Noble Phantasm?"::
22475::$$$message_0177_0034_0000$$$::"Hm? No, it's free. You don't need to give anything up. I'm aligned with the nothingness of the void. I can come back to life, so long as I'm nothing.[lr]::
22476::$$$message_0177_0034_0001$$$::You can rest easy and just keep trying until you believe me."::
22477::$$$message_0177_0035_0000$$$::"...I've verified that as long as I'm contracted with you, I cannot lose."[lr]::
22478::$$$message_0177_0035_0001$$$::Yep. Though you can't win, either.::
22479::$$$message_0177_0036_0000$$$::"That just leaves one question... [cacheimage storage=バゼット04g(中)][wvl canskip=0 time=400][chgfg time=300 storage=バゼット04g(中)]No, why am I complaining when circumstances are already this favorable?"[lr]::
22480::$$$message_0177_0036_0001$$$::"Hm? What's the matter now? Did you want to ask something else?"::
22481::$$$message_0177_0037_0000$$$::"Ngh... This might be a silly question...[lr]::
22482::$$$message_0177_0037_0001$$$::It's amazing that you can resurrect me when I die. One might even say it breaks the rules."::
22483::$$$message_0177_0038_0000$$$::"But, um...[lr]::
22484::$$$message_0177_0038_0001$$$::Will it always hurt that much every time? I know I get to escape death, but the thought of that agony makes me think twice..."[lr]::
22485::$$$message_0177_0038_0002$$$::"Huh? What, are you afraid of coming back to life?"::
22486::$$$message_0177_0039_0000$$$::"I'm not a-afraid! I'm just saying that it feels unpleasant![lr]::
22487::$$$message_0177_0039_0001$$$::...I don't know if 'hell' is the right word for it, but it made me feel filthy.[lr]::
22488::$$$message_0177_0039_0002$$$::The dead aren't supposed to be conscious. A regular dead person wouldn't feel anything about it, but someone conscious would feel utter torment."::
22489::$$$message_0177_0040_0000$$$::"Ahh... [wvl canskip=false time=800]You're right.[lr]::
22490::$$$message_0177_0040_0001$$$::Well, shit. It doesn't feel like anything special to me. I just woke up feeling this way. It might be because you're human, and I'm a Servant. Though..."[lr]::
22491::$$$message_0177_0040_0002$$$::Gotta at least put up with this much.[lr]::
22492::$$$message_0177_0040_0003$$$::After all, she's basically a dead woman walking.::
22493::$$$message_0177_0041_0000$$$::"Ain't you a little demanding right now?"::
22494::$$$message_0177_0042_0000$$$::"Ngh... I-I know. It's just how I feel.[lr]::
22495::$$$message_0177_0042_0001$$$::If this torture is the price for resurrection, then I'll just have to pay it."[lr]::
22496::$$$message_0177_0042_0002$$$::"Yeah! It won't be the last time, so get used to it."::
22497::$$$message_0177_0043_0000$$$::"Hmph. As if I would die that many times.[r]::
22498::$$$message_0177_0043_0001$$$::Saber will be the next to die. I'll impale her through the chest, just like she did to me."[lr]::
22499::$$$message_0177_0043_0002$$$::"Yep, that's my Master.[lr]::
22500::$$$message_0177_0043_0003$$$::Guess we'd better get back to the Holy Grail War while we're still fired up."[wvs][clfg textoff=0 pos=all rule=シャッター左から time=400]::
22501::$$$message_0177_0044_0000$$$::I head for the exit.[lr]::
22502::$$$message_0177_0044_0001$$$::To be honest, I couldn't give a rat's ass about the Holy Grail War, but I don't like the idea of just sitting and taking it, either.::
22503::$$$message_0177_0045_0000$$$::Gotta find an enemy to kill as soon as I can.[lr]::
22504::$$$message_0177_0045_0001$$$::I'll kill whoever hurts me.[lr]::
22505::$$$message_0177_0045_0002$$$::I'll kill whoever didn't stop themselves from hurting me.[lr]::
22506::$$$message_0177_0045_0003$$$::Anyone I see'll die. I'll kill any humans that are alive.[lr]::
22507::$$$message_0177_0045_0004$$$::Otherwise, I can't stay insane.[lr]::
22508::$$$message_0177_0045_0005$$$::Otherwise, I'll lose my mind.::
22509::$$$message_0177_0046_0000$$$::"What's up? Aren't we going, Master?"[lr]::
22510::$$$message_0177_0046_0001$$$::I swallow my heart that threatens to leap out of my mouth, and turn back to Bazett, who's just standing there.[lr]::
22511::$$$message_0177_0046_0002$$$::Did she remember my bloodlust?[lr]::
22512::$$$message_0177_0046_0003$$$::She's making the same face she did when I attacked those bloody houses.::
22513::$$$message_0177_0047_0000$$$::"...I still have much to learn. Why didn't I remember the most important question?"[lr]::
22514::$$$message_0177_0047_0001$$$::It's obvious.[lr]::
22515::$$$message_0177_0047_0002$$$::You didn't remember because you don't want to remember.::
22516::$$$message_0177_0048_0000$$$::"Answer me. What Servant are you?"[lr]::
22517::$$$message_0177_0048_0001$$$::Hostility taints the question.[lr]::
22518::$$$message_0177_0048_0002$$$::Then, I grin like a girl waiting for her lover, and say...[current withback=false][wt canskip=0][stopdash][lr]::
22519::$$$message_0177_0048_0003$$$::"Avenger. The Servant of vengeance."[lr]::
22520::$$$message_0177_0048_0004$$$::With hatred and joy, I declare a class which doesn't exist.::
22521::$$$message_0177_0049_0000$$$::It's a high-speed combo.[lr]::
22522::$$$message_0177_0049_0001$$$::The right straight mercilessly crushes a monster's skull with inhuman savagery, enough to make one pity the enemy.[lr]::
22523::$$$message_0177_0049_0002$$$::Ten of their number have already died to vengeance, but more prey rise to meet her.[lr]::
22524::$$$message_0177_0049_0003$$$::Venomous, cursed claws target her during the brief instant after she pulls her right fist back, hoping to wound her before she regains her balance!::
22525::$$$message_0177_0050_0000$$$::She evades them with a light shake of the head, simultaneously lashing out at another monster's temple with her right foot.[lr]::
22526::$$$message_0177_0050_0001$$$::Sharp and heavy.[lr]::
22527::$$$message_0177_0050_0002$$$::A head, wet like a tomato, goes flying.[lr]::
22528::$$$message_0177_0050_0003$$$::Without visually confirming the kill, Bazett whirls on another prey approaching from behind, intercepting it with lethal timing.::
22529::$$$message_0177_0051_0000$$$::    She's like a bladed comet.[lr]::
22530::$$$message_0177_0051_0001$$$::She cuts down attackers from every direction like a ruthless, four-handed danse macabre.::
22531::$$$message_0177_0052_0000$$$::"Hot damn. I barely get to show off at all."[wvs][wsplinemove canskip=0][shock vmax=20 hmax=20 time=600 count=3][se storage=se094.wav][lr]::
22532::$$$message_0177_0052_0001$$$::I'm doing all right in my corner, but for every one beast I kill, Bazett pulverizes three.[lr]::
22533::$$$message_0177_0052_0002$$$::I mean, she [font italic=true]literally[font italic=false] pulverizes them. She's a walking meat grinder despite those thin arms and legs.::
22534::$$$message_0177_0053_0000$$$::I really underestimated her. Who thought that humans could take unarmed combat to this level?[lr]::
22535::$$$message_0177_0053_0001$$$::Her fists, feet, knees, and elbows appear to be inscribed with Runes of hardening, but her basic fighting moves must be based on refined fighting techniques meant for humans to use.[lr]::
22536::$$$message_0177_0053_0002$$$::It's nothing like the way I give myself over to my instincts to lash out at my enemies.::
22537::$$$message_0177_0054_0000$$$::Bazett's moves are the result of generations of blood and sweat.[lr]::
22538::$$$message_0177_0054_0001$$$::I wonder how much time and effort it took to hone them to this level. She's a young girl, I mean, a mature woman, so has she even had time to learn anything else? Probably not.[lr]::
22539::$$$message_0177_0054_0002$$$::The monsters are no match for this human weapon.[lr]::
22540::$$$message_0177_0054_0003$$$::They're just sheep to be hunted, prey trying to find safety in numbers. I guess they've just got a rendezvous with fate.[lr]::
22541::$$$message_0177_0054_0004$$$::You ever wonder where the French put their silent letters? Probably up their a[line len=2]::
22542::$$$message_0177_0055_0000$$$::"I see. So this is the 'bizarre bunch' you mentioned."[lr]::
22543::$$$message_0177_0055_0001$$$::Bazett exhales loudly and puts away her gloves.[lr]::
22544::$$$message_0177_0055_0002$$$::I can't believe it. She's taken out nearly twenty of those things, and all she has to say is 'whew'...!?::
22545::$$$message_0177_0056_0000$$$::"...They must be familiars of some kind.[lr]::
22546::$$$message_0177_0056_0001$$$::They seem unintelligent and specialized at killing humans, but are suited to be commanded en masse.[lr]::
22547::$$$message_0177_0056_0002$$$::Clearly, there is an eighth mage at work who is not a Master... A mage who attacks people indiscriminately with familiars can't be ignored.[lr]::
22548::$$$message_0177_0056_0003$$$::Do you have any idea who they might be?"[lr]::
22549::$$$message_0177_0056_0004$$$::"Huh? Me?"::
22550::$$$message_0177_0057_0000$$$::"Hmm. No one comes to mind. We'll probably run into them sooner or later, though."[lr]::
22551::$$$message_0177_0057_0001$$$::After all, we've got all the time in the world.[lr]::
22552::$$$message_0177_0057_0002$$$::It won't end no matter what we do, so we're bound to encounter them at some point.::
22553::$$$message_0177_0058_0000$$$::"...Very well. I apologize for doubting you. The abnormalities in this city must be the work of the monsters' master, not you."::
22554::$$$message_0177_0059_0000$$$::"It's fine. I'm used to false accusations, and we're two birds of a feather anyway.[lr]::
22555::$$$message_0177_0059_0001$$$::It's just a matter of whether they acted first or me.[lr]::
22556::$$$message_0177_0059_0002$$$::These things have been killing people all over the city, leaving me with nothing to do."::
22557::$$$message_0177_0060_0000$$$::I'm glad they saved me the work, but it's never a good feeling to have someone steal your job. It impinges on my raison d'etre. I can't bear the thought of being a deadbeat.::
22558::$$$message_0177_0061_0000$$$::"...Stop that. I don't know what Heroic Spirit you are, but as long as you're my Servant, I will not allow you to involve ordinary people."[lr]::
22559::$$$message_0177_0061_0001$$$::"Like I said, I didn't kill anyone today. I was drooling over that street stall guy earlier but I still didn't touch him, you know.[lr]::
22560::$$$message_0177_0061_0002$$$::I sure wanted some of that oden and meat. But I'm a dog who does what he's told. C'mon, tell me I'm a good boy."::
22561::$$$message_0177_0062_0000$$$::"That's expected of you. I don't need to compliment you for it."[lr]::
22562::$$$message_0177_0062_0001$$$::Got me a hard-to-please owner.[lr]::
22563::$$$message_0177_0062_0002$$$::Makes me wanna rebel at any moment.::
22564::$$$message_0177_0063_0000$$$::"More importantly, we need to make something clear.[lr]::
22565::$$$message_0177_0063_0001$$$::I know what your Noble Phantasm does, but you still haven't told me your True Name.[lr]::
22566::$$$message_0177_0063_0002$$$::Where is your legend from? What Heroic Spirit are you?"[lr]::
22567::$$$message_0177_0063_0003$$$::"I told you that right away.[l][say storage=snplg02_anr_0251 name=アンリ] It's your fault for not remembering, but oh yeah, your memory is still foggy."::
22568::$$$message_0177_0064_0000$$$::"I... Yes, I may as well admit it.[lr]::
22569::$$$message_0177_0064_0001$$$::Avenger, I don't remember making a pact with you. I thought my memory would recover given time, but the situation appears to be worse than I thought. I don't know how long it will take for my memories to return."::
22570::$$$message_0177_0065_0000$$$::"So you want me to explain again.[lr]::
22571::$$$message_0177_0065_0001$$$::Still, I don't know much.[lr]::
22572::$$$message_0177_0065_0002$$$::You summoned me as a Servant and made a pact with me.[lr]::
22573::$$$message_0177_0065_0003$$$::When I came to, I was in the mansion, and you had me collared and doing your bidding.[lr]::
22574::$$$message_0177_0065_0004$$$::That's when I told you my True Name... Well, it's not like it matters if you ask."::
22575::$$$message_0177_0066_0000$$$::"Not like it matters? What do you mean[line len=2]"[lr]::
22576::$$$message_0177_0066_0001$$$::"I don't have a name of my own. I don't know what my name was when I was alive."::
22577::$$$message_0177_0067_0000$$$::"That's absurd! You're a Servant, so you must be a Heroic Spirit! There's no such thing as a nameless hero!"[lr]::
22578::$$$message_0177_0067_0001$$$::"Yeah. So I have a name, but it wasn't my name as a human. I can tell you what people called me, if you want."::
22579::$$$message_0177_0068_0000$$$::"...Of course I want that. I should have heard your name when we made the contract.[lr]::
22580::$$$message_0177_0068_0001$$$::That's why I trust... No, that's how I decided that you were suitable to help me win the Holy Grail War.[lr]::
22581::$$$message_0177_0068_0002$$$::So, what name did you give me?"[lr]::
22582::$$$message_0177_0068_0003$$$::"Aŋra Mainiiu. It's a name from an old tradition, in some faraway land."[cacheimage storage=バゼット02b(中)][wvs][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=バゼット02b(中)]::
22583::$$$message_0177_0069_0000$$$::No point hiding it.[lr]::
22584::$$$message_0177_0069_0001$$$::It's nothing to be pretentious about, so I just tell her.::
22585::$$$message_0177_0070_0000$$$::"Aŋra Mainiiu... That name is..."[lr]::
22586::$$$message_0177_0070_0001$$$::That isn't a hero's name.[lr]::
22587::$$$message_0177_0070_0002$$$::It isn't worthy of a hero.[lr]::
22588::$$$message_0177_0070_0003$$$::It isn't even something you should call a person.[lr]::
22589::$$$message_0177_0070_0004$$$::Her face says it all, and more.[lr]::
22590::$$$message_0177_0070_0005$$$::I know how my noble Master must feel right now. I totally fail to live up to my name.::
22591::$$$message_0177_0071_0000$$$::Aŋra Mainiiu is the name of one of the greatest devils of ancient Persia.[lr]::
22592::$$$message_0177_0071_0001$$$::It was the biggest antagonist of Zoroastrianism, an advocate of evil said to be fighting the light god and guardian of human benevolence for nine thousand years.[lr]::
22593::$$$message_0177_0071_0002$$$::In short, a god of evil.[lr]::
22594::$$$message_0177_0071_0003$$$::On top of that, its domain encompasses half of the entire world. Just the fact that I was named thusly invites trouble.[lr]::
22595::$$$message_0177_0071_0004$$$::...Honestly, I'd feel a lot less inadequate if it was something more modest, like the god of desks or jars.::
22596::$$$message_0177_0072_0000$$$::Zoroastrianism revolves around the conflict between the gods of good and evil. It's one of the world's first religions which inspired the duality between angels and demons.[lr]::
22597::$$$message_0177_0072_0001$$$::Of course, I've never seen any angels or known any demons.[lr]::
22598::$$$message_0177_0072_0002$$$::I was just one person in a village of people who got all hot and bothered about those teachings. They treated me as a hero for just a bit of sin and salvation, and apparently, enshrined me as a Heroic Spirit after I died.[wt canskip=0][wm canskip=0][stopdash][current withback=false]::
22599::$$$message_0177_0073_0000$$$::"Don't get the wrong idea. I'm not an actual god.[lr]::
22600::$$$message_0177_0073_0001$$$::I probably just happened to have a similar attribute to it, so they gave me that name.[lr]::
22601::$$$message_0177_0073_0002$$$::I'm a low-caliber Heroic Spirit, and as you know, a useless third-rate Servant."::
22602::$$$message_0177_0074_0000$$$::"I'm well aware. I won't ask you to defend yourself now."[lr]::
22603::$$$message_0177_0074_0001$$$::Hahaha. You really are a tough audience, Master.::
22604::$$$message_0177_0075_0000$$$::"Still...Aŋra Mainiiu. No, I'm sure the Servant I meant to summon was..."[lr]::
22605::$$$message_0177_0075_0001$$$::She mumbles about how it feels like someone that was important to her.[lr]::
22606::$$$message_0177_0075_0002$$$::Bazett Fraga McRemitz questions herself.::
22607::$$$message_0177_0076_0000$$$::"Hmm. Someone dear to you.[lr]::
22608::$$$message_0177_0076_0001$$$::Were you trying to call some other Heroic Spirit? Not me, but some really strong, magnificent hero?"::
22609::$$$message_0177_0077_0000$$$::"Huh...? [cacheimage storage=バゼット04g(中)][wvl canskip=0 time=500][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=バゼット04g(中)]N-no, not really..."[lr]::
22610::$$$message_0177_0077_0001$$$::I hear her whisper "...well."[lr]::
22611::$$$message_0177_0077_0002$$$::Wow, that tells me everything I need to know. She's got someone else on her mind...which I knew, but who knew she'd be this picky about Servants![lr]::
22612::$$$message_0177_0077_0003$$$::Tch. So she compromised to get me. [l]And here I was pretty serious. [l]Well, whatever.::
22613::$$$message_0177_0078_0000$$$::"That's a funny face. You can look like that too, huh? It's kinda a let down, but I expected this.[lr]::
22614::$$$message_0177_0078_0001$$$::So, what kind of guy is your type?"[lr]::
22615::$$$message_0177_0078_0002$$$::"W-what are you talking about? We aren't discussing my taste in men! I was just thinking that you're different from the hero I had in mind."::
22616::$$$message_0177_0079_0000$$$::"Yeah, and what's he like? A familiar is supposed to represent the spellcaster's preference, so I'd expect a female Master to summon some hot guy.[lr]::
22617::$$$message_0177_0079_0001$$$::Oh. Or were you trying to summon a woman? [wvl canskip=0 time=800]That's...deep. Don't tell me you were cross-dressing for both business and pleasure."::
22618::$$$message_0177_0080_0000$$$::"I have no such proclivities. I made a pact with you because I judged it the correct course of action. It has nothing to do with any feeling for the opposite sex.[lr]::
22619::$$$message_0177_0080_0001$$$::...However, I admit that what I said was misleading. Yes, I was fixated on a Heroic Spirit other than you."::
22620::$$$message_0177_0081_0000$$$::"Yeah, that. You might as well tell me the rest. Nothing to lose, so let's keep as few secrets as we can.[lr]::
22621::$$$message_0177_0081_0001$$$::So, Master. Which Heroic Spirit were you trying to summon?"::
22622::$$$message_0177_0082_0000$$$::"...I wasn't exactly trying to summon him.[lr]::
22623::$$$message_0177_0082_0001$$$::There was no guarantee I could summon him, since I didn't believe he actually existed."[lr]::
22624::$$$message_0177_0082_0002$$$::Her voice grows timid, uncertain.[lr]::
22625::$$$message_0177_0082_0003$$$::She must be reliving an old memory.[lr]::
22626::$$$message_0177_0082_0004$$$::She shrinks back, as if admonishing herself.::
22627::$$$message_0177_0083_0000$$$::"I see. You can't summon a hero you don't believe in. But you wanted to meet him."[lr]::
22628::$$$message_0177_0083_0001$$$::"...I'm not sure. It's embarrassing to talk about, but I'm not sure myself."::
22629::$$$message_0177_0084_0000$$$::"...This is about my childhood.[lr]::
22630::$$$message_0177_0084_0001$$$::I was, um, a cold child, towards everything.[lr]::
22631::$$$message_0177_0084_0002$$$::I couldn't really understand what people around me called 'fun,' and I often troubled my parents.[lr]::
22632::$$$message_0177_0084_0003$$$::...My father once said that I spent my entire day like I was working. He often apologized to me, all while looking guilty."[wt canskip=0][current withback=false]::
22633::$$$message_0177_0085_0000$$$::"I think only my parents felt any guilt.[lr]::
22634::$$$message_0177_0085_0001$$$::I never sensed the way my father felt, and the days passed in tedium, like they do now.[lr]::
22635::$$$message_0177_0085_0002$$$::Most of my memories are of those bland days.[lr]::
22636::$$$message_0177_0085_0003$$$::But there was one thing I was obsessed with.[lr]::
22637::$$$message_0177_0085_0004$$$::Even now, I'm not sure if it was really that special. I read a storybook I happened to find in my family's library, about an old story of my country, and it made me very sad."::
22638::$$$message_0177_0086_0000$$$::"...An old story. So that's it."[lr]::
22639::$$$message_0177_0086_0001$$$::It's hard to believe, but that's who she wanted to meet.[lr]::
22640::$$$message_0177_0086_0002$$$::A young girl dreamed and forgot it as she grew up. Just one of life's many abandoned fantasies.::
22641::$$$message_0177_0087_0000$$$::"...Yes. Just during this short period of my childhood, I was like the other children my age. A heroic tale captured my heart.[lr]::
22642::$$$message_0177_0087_0001$$$::But the tale didn't have a pretty ending. It certainly wasn't a story worth praising."::
22643::$$$message_0177_0088_0000$$$::"...Everyone said it was a tale of valor, but I couldn't see it that way. That's when I began to think that I wanted to save him.[lr]::
22644::$$$message_0177_0088_0001$$$::...It's not as if I could actually do anything, but I wished that it could be so."::
22645::$$$message_0177_0089_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
22646::$$$message_0177_0089_0001$$$::Generally, humans have an urge to save things, and most of 'em like that idea.[lr]::
22647::$$$message_0177_0089_0002$$$::Even I harbor similar feelings.[lr]::
22648::$$$message_0177_0089_0003$$$::No matter what form that desire takes, you can't blame her for at least feeling that way.[lr]::
22649::$$$message_0177_0089_0004$$$::However...::
22650::$$$message_0177_0090_0000$$$::                                     [font italic=true]Am I really allowed to wish for that?[font italic=false]::
22651::$$$message_0177_0091_0000$$$::The answer might be clear to the rest of us, but it wasn't for that little girl.[lr]::
22652::$$$message_0177_0091_0001$$$::Bazett wished for something that anyone could do.[lr]::
22653::$$$message_0177_0091_0002$$$::She wanted to save a hero from a fairy tale, the only person she ever acknowledged.[lr]::
22654::$$$message_0177_0091_0003$$$::"...Ha."[lr]::
22655::$$$message_0177_0091_0004$$$::No "whatever" from me this time.[lr]::
22656::$$$message_0177_0091_0005$$$::[noise opacity=90]Bastard, I'll kill you if I ever see you.[stopnoise]::
22657::$$$message_0177_0092_0000$$$::"Awfully selfless of you. So is that your wish? Seems like a pretty cheap thing to use the Holy Grail on."[lr]::
22658::$$$message_0177_0092_0001$$$::I snicker.[lr]::
22659::$$$message_0177_0092_0002$$$::It's pretty funny, actually. Like pitting two fairy tales against each other.::
22660::$$$message_0177_0093_0000$$$::"I-I told you, that was just while I was a child. I was only saying that's the Heroic Spirit I would choose to summon now.[lr]::
22661::$$$message_0177_0093_0001$$$::It would be my motive for summoning him, if I had a catalyst that could call him forth."[lr]::
22662::$$$message_0177_0093_0002$$$::"Hahaha. But you got a punk like me, instead. You've got rotten luck with men, Master!"::
22663::$$$message_0177_0094_0000$$$::I cackle.[lr]::
22664::$$$message_0177_0094_0001$$$::Seriously, she's one unlucky lady.::
22665::$$$message_0177_0095_0000$$$::"Avenger. My desire is to secure the Holy Grail and bring it back to the Mage's Association. I have no wish to use on the Grail itself."[lr]::
22666::$$$message_0177_0095_0001$$$::"I know. You aren't cunning enough for that."[lr]::
22667::$$$message_0177_0095_0002$$$::You can't wish for what doesn't exist, anyway.[lr]::
22668::$$$message_0177_0095_0003$$$::Zero times anything is still zero.::
22669::$$$message_0177_0096_0000$$$::"...Now it's your turn, Avenger. I answered your questions. Tell me what your wish is."[lr]::
22670::$$$message_0177_0096_0001$$$::"Eh?"[lr]::
22671::$$$message_0177_0096_0002$$$::Damn, she turned the tables on me.[lr]::
22672::$$$message_0177_0096_0003$$$::The truth is, I don't have a wish for the Holy Grail, just like my Master.[lr]::
22673::$$$message_0177_0096_0004$$$::I think it's a little tragic that there's only one thing I'm obsessed with right now.::
22674::$$$message_0177_0097_0000$$$::"My wish?[lr]::
22675::$$$message_0177_0097_0001$$$::Hmm, if I had to say, I guess I want to finish a picture."[lr]::
22676::$$$message_0177_0097_0002$$$::Heh heh. Her face says she has no idea what I'm talking about.[lr]::
22677::$$$message_0177_0097_0003$$$::After this, when we go back to the hideout and she finds the unfinished sliding puzzle I'm working on, she'll get pissed off and tell me to answer the question.::
22678::$$$message_0177_0098_0000$$$::"...Wait. Did you feel that wave of strong magical energy?"[lr]::
22679::$$$message_0177_0098_0001$$$::"Sorry, I can't detect magical energy. But I saw where it came from. Something just lit up on top of that building."[lr]::
22680::$$$message_0177_0098_0002$$$::Bazett reacts quickly.[lr]::
22681::$$$message_0177_0098_0003$$$::She shoulders the pack that was resting at her feet, tells me to keep up, and starts running for the Center Building.::
22682::$$$message_0177_0099_0000$$$::I follow her dutifully.[lr]::
22683::$$$message_0177_0099_0001$$$::Still...[lr]::
22684::$$$message_0177_0099_0002$$$::I'm a little curious.[lr]::
22685::$$$message_0177_0099_0003$$$::I wanna know what that tube on her back is.[lr]::
22686::$$$message_0177_0099_0004$$$::It's gotta have some kinda weapon, but she tossed it on the ground and didn't use it during the fight earlier.[lr]::
22687::$$$message_0177_0099_0005$$$::You can't blame me for being curious after seeing her pick it back up.::
22688::$$$message_0177_0100_0000$$$::"Hey, what's that?"[lr]::
22689::$$$message_0177_0100_0001$$$::"..."[lr]::
22690::$$$message_0177_0100_0002$$$::Bazett searches for a back entrance to the building. She looks very tense.[lr]::
22691::$$$message_0177_0100_0003$$$::"Hey, hey. What's that you're carrying?"[lr]::
22692::$$$message_0177_0100_0004$$$::I pester her just as tenaciously.[lr]::
22693::$$$message_0177_0100_0005$$$::"...Haah."[lr]::
22694::$$$message_0177_0100_0006$$$::Maybe it worked, because she stops and shows me the tube.::
22695::$$$message_0177_0101_0000$$$::I examine it for about one minute.[lr]::
22696::$$$message_0177_0101_0001$$$::After waiting for me to get a good look, she says,[lr]::
22697::$$$message_0177_0101_0002$$$::"So? Do you know now?"[lr]::
22698::$$$message_0177_0101_0003$$$::"Yeah, got it. There's probably a tea set in there."[lr]::
22699::$$$message_0177_0101_0004$$$::"..."[lr]::
22700::$$$message_0177_0101_0005$$$::Oh, she mad.[lr]::
22701::$$$message_0177_0101_0006$$$::Bazett's brow furrows, and she reluctantly removes a lid from the cylinder.::
22702::$$$message_0177_0102_0000$$$::Balls roll out of it.[lr]::
22703::$$$message_0177_0102_0001$$$::They're about as big and heavy as shot put balls. The tube looks like it could fit up to five, but there's only three inside.::
22704::$$$message_0177_0103_0000$$$::I see. Now I understand everything.[lr]::
22705::$$$message_0177_0103_0001$$$::Bazett Fraga McRemitz is someone to be feared, if she's carrying [font italic=true]these[font italic=false] things around.[lr]::
22706::$$$message_0177_0103_0002$$$::By the way,[lr]::
22707::$$$message_0177_0103_0003$$$::"What are these?"[lr]::
22708::$$$message_0177_0103_0004$$$::The mystery only deepens.::
22709::$$$message_0177_0104_0000$$$::"I won't explain it to you. I just wanted you to know that it isn't a tea set."[lr]::
22710::$$$message_0177_0104_0001$$$::She puts the balls back into the tube and shoulders it again.[lr]::
22711::$$$message_0177_0104_0002$$$::Probably doesn't wanna put all her cards on the table with someone she doesn't trust.[lr]::
22712::$$$message_0177_0104_0003$$$::That's fine.::
22713::$$$message_0177_0105_0000$$$::"You're pretty brawny. What, are your shoulder muscles strong because your boobs are so heavy? Man, it's such a waste since you don't flaunt whatcha got."[cacheimage storage=バゼット02d(遠)][wvs][fg opacity=0 textoff=0 left=234 index=2000 top=83 time=100 storage=バゼット02d(遠)][lr]::
22714::$$$message_0177_0105_0001$$$::I state the objective facts, with my well-honed eye for beauty.[lr]::
22715::$$$message_0177_0105_0002$$$::Bazett skids to a halt, and slowly turns around like a rusty mechanical doll.[wm canskip=0]::
22716::$$$message_0177_0106_0000$$$::"...How delightful. Your rapier wit can be so bold that it makes me want to kill someone."[lr]::
22717::$$$message_0177_0106_0001$$$::I like the edge in her voice.[lr]::
22718::$$$message_0177_0106_0002$$$::This is how a Master and Servant should be.[lr]::
22719::$$$message_0177_0106_0003$$$::Her tension practically spells out how she's going to murder me if we survive the night.::
22720::$$$message_0177_0107_0000$$$::There's nobody on the rooftop.[lr]::
22721::$$$message_0177_0107_0001$$$::We take in the howling wind.::
22722::$$$message_0177_0108_0000$$$::"...We're too late. There are clear signs that someone was here, but it won't be possible to locate them on foot."[lr]::
22723::$$$message_0177_0108_0001$$$::Bazett walks to the edge and looks down, looking for clues.::
22724::$$$message_0177_0109_0000$$$::As for me...[lr]::
22725::$$$message_0177_0109_0001$$$::I rub out the bloodstains on the ground with my feet.::
22726::$$$message_0177_0110_0000$$$::This is the highest vantage point in Shinto.[lr]::
22727::$$$message_0177_0110_0001$$$::The moon seems closer here, so much so that it feels like you could reach it with a ladder or a set of stairs.::
22728::$$$message_0177_0111_0000$$$::The city is mostly empty by now, but is still lit up.[lr]::
22729::$$$message_0177_0111_0001$$$::I gaze out at the dazzling indicator of prosperity.[lr]::
22730::$$$message_0177_0111_0002$$$::   This won't be boring, no.[lr]::
22731::$$$message_0177_0111_0003$$$::It's nothing special, but I have nothing bad to say about this vista.::
22732::$$$message_0177_0112_0000$$$::"...Avenger."[lr]::
22733::$$$message_0177_0112_0001$$$::Her voice cuts through the night.[lr]::
22734::$$$message_0177_0112_0002$$$::Bazett walks up next to me.::
22735::$$$message_0177_0113_0000$$$::"What? Find anything useful?"[lr]::
22736::$$$message_0177_0113_0001$$$::"I just identified several more monsters. I think I can spot any familiars in Shinto with the naked eye from here."[lr]::
22737::$$$message_0177_0113_0002$$$::She gives me a meaningful glance.[lr]::
22738::$$$message_0177_0113_0003$$$::Apparently, she was watching the monsters roaming the city, not taking in the sights.::
22739::$$$message_0177_0114_0000$$$::"So what? Are you going to stake them out from up here and try to find their master?"[lr]::
22740::$$$message_0177_0114_0001$$$::"Realistically, no. The familiars are expendable. They won't return to their owner, so we won't be able to find their home base from here."[lr]::
22741::$$$message_0177_0114_0002$$$::"Yeah. Let's not waste time. I'm glad to have such a wise Master. But if you're saying that..."::
22742::$$$message_0177_0115_0000$$$::"Avenger, I want to purge the city of those monsters.[lr]::
22743::$$$message_0177_0115_0001$$$::I need your help to do that."[lr]::
22744::$$$message_0177_0115_0002$$$::"..."[lr]::
22745::$$$message_0177_0115_0003$$$::There it is.[lr]::
22746::$$$message_0177_0115_0004$$$::Good god, this is the problem with overachievers.[lr]::
22747::$$$message_0177_0115_0005$$$::Makes me want to tear her limb from limb.::
22748::$$$message_0177_0116_0000$$$::"It's an easier order to follow than telling me not to involve bystanders. Are you sure, Master? I thought your goal was to win the war.[lr]::
22749::$$$message_0177_0116_0001$$$::I get that their master is an obstacle. But it doesn't make sense to get rid of them just because they're killing people. First you talk like you're some bad bitch, and now you want to be a goody-two-shoes. Pretty self-serving."::
22750::$$$message_0177_0117_0000$$$::This time, I don't bother hiding my bloodlust, making it clear that this could turn into a bloodbath.[lr]::
22751::$$$message_0177_0117_0001$$$::I move my hand behind me and summon my favorite dagger.[lr]::
22752::$$$message_0177_0117_0002$$$::My prediction[line len=2]that we'd end up trying to kill each other at least once[line len=2]looks about to come true. Someone call me a prophet.::
22753::$$$message_0177_0118_0000$$$::I won't be the one to start it, but I'll answer if she comes at me. That's my style.[lr]::
22754::$$$message_0177_0118_0001$$$::Very regrettable, but it had to happen at[line len=2]huh?::
22755::$$$message_0177_0119_0000$$$::"You're right.[lr]::
22756::$$$message_0177_0119_0001$$$::My goal isn't to save people."[lr]::
22757::$$$message_0177_0119_0002$$$::She shows a moment's hesitation.[lr]::
22758::$$$message_0177_0119_0003$$$::Then wisely swallows it.[lr]::
22759::$$$message_0177_0119_0004$$$::"But I want to right this wrong.[lr]::
22760::$$$message_0177_0119_0005$$$::I can't ignore this now that I've seen it."[lr]::
22761::$$$message_0177_0119_0006$$$::She sounds like she's trying to convince herself.::
22762::$$$message_0177_0120_0000$$$::"...Hmm. What for?[lr]::
22763::$$$message_0177_0120_0001$$$::You don't wanna let them kill people?[lr]::
22764::$$$message_0177_0120_0002$$$::You don't wanna be someone who lets that happen?[lr]::
22765::$$$message_0177_0120_0003$$$::Or...[l][say storage=snplg02_anr_0554 name=アンリ]you care more about helping people than winning the Holy Grail War?"::
22766::$$$message_0177_0121_0000$$$::All of the above, probably.[lr]::
22767::$$$message_0177_0121_0001$$$::That's why Bazett's bound by all these contradictory desires.[lr]::
22768::$$$message_0177_0121_0002$$$::If she believed she was right, she wouldn't be struggling this much. She's desperately trying to repress the side of her that's a mage.::
22769::$$$message_0177_0122_0000$$$::"I have no reason to believe I'm correct.[lr]::
22770::$$$message_0177_0122_0001$$$::...But I think there has to be a reason. I feel like it's the right thing to do, so..."[lr]::
22771::$$$message_0177_0122_0002$$$::She probably wants to say that there isn't a contradiction between the benefit and her motives.::
22772::$$$message_0177_0123_0000$$$::"...Wow. Talk about self-righteous. That's crazy talk."[lr]::
22773::$$$message_0177_0123_0001$$$::"Yes. I'm well aware."[lr]::
22774::$$$message_0177_0123_0002$$$::She's clapping back.[lr]::
22775::$$$message_0177_0123_0003$$$::That's probably the idea of righteousness she wants to believe in.[lr]::
22776::$$$message_0177_0123_0004$$$::On the other hand, as she is right now, Bazett Fraga McRemitz is a slave to the Association's motives.[lr]::
22777::$$$message_0177_0123_0005$$$::I wonder how long she can keep playing both sides.::
22778::$$$message_0177_0124_0000$$$::"Very noble and all, but do you really have to take the moral high ground here?[lr]::
22779::$$$message_0177_0124_0001$$$::It doesn't have a shape. No matter how much you woo it, it won't put out. Why don't you just throw in with a faction that'll treat you better?"::
22780::$$$message_0177_0125_0000$$$::"...As I said, I belong to the Mage's Association.[lr]::
22781::$$$message_0177_0125_0001$$$::I want to be compensated. [l][say storage=snplg02_baz_0632 name=バゼット]But separately from that, I also want to make the right choices, when I can."::
22782::$$$message_0177_0126_0000$$$::Wonder why she feels that way.[lr]::
22783::$$$message_0177_0126_0001$$$::It implies that there are times when she thinks she's in the wrong.[lr]::
22784::$$$message_0177_0126_0002$$$::She's trying to clean the dirty parts of herself by making better choices.::
22785::$$$message_0177_0127_0000$$$::Man...[lr]::
22786::$$$message_0177_0127_0001$$$::"...You sure sound like a straight shooter.[lr]::
22787::$$$message_0177_0127_0002$$$::Aiming to be a paragon of virtue."[lr]::
22788::$$$message_0177_0127_0003$$$::What an awkward, pathetic life she must live.::
22789::$$$message_0177_0128_0000$$$::"...Yes, perhaps.[lr]::
22790::$$$message_0177_0128_0001$$$::But that's a wish that won't come true. All I do is destroy, and no one will thank me for it. Virtue is reserved for those who can befriend and be befriended by others.[lr]::
22791::$$$message_0177_0128_0002$$$::It's something I'll never have."::
22792::$$$message_0177_0129_0000$$$::Virtue is about contributing to society and helping other people.[lr]::
22793::$$$message_0177_0129_0001$$$::She says that she can only destroy.[lr]::
22794::$$$message_0177_0129_0002$$$::She's convinced that someone who can't mend or create can never truly earn the trust of others.::
22795::$$$message_0177_0130_0000$$$::"I think you're wrong about that."[lr]::
22796::$$$message_0177_0130_0001$$$::"No. I can't relinquish my wealth to help the poor, nor can I create a new organization. I can't escape the fact that I'm just a puny, single gear in a machine.[lr]::
22797::$$$message_0177_0130_0002$$$::...There's no way someone like me can ever gain virtue."::
22798::$$$message_0177_0131_0000$$$::"No way."[lr]::
22799::$$$message_0177_0131_0001$$$::Hell, I'm actually getting mad now.[lr]::
22800::$$$message_0177_0131_0002$$$::Ugh. I'm taking this way too seriously.::
22801::$$$message_0177_0132_0000$$$::"That's a load of horse shit. Money can't buy virtue.[lr]::
22802::$$$message_0177_0132_0001$$$::Virtue is a quality of the soul. It isn't something you acquire. You cultivate it while you suffer."[lr]::
22803::$$$message_0177_0132_0002$$$::"..."::
22804::$$$message_0177_0133_0000$$$::That's true of every human, no matter how insignificant, powerless, or worthless one is.[lr]::
22805::$$$message_0177_0133_0001$$$::It's a function everyone possesses equally at birth, a radiance that grows according to one's will to move forward.[lr]::
22806::$$$message_0177_0133_0002$$$::...It doesn't distinguish between good or evil.[lr]::
22807::$$$message_0177_0133_0003$$$::It's like a greater understanding you can only gain on your own, available to only those who aim for ever greater heights as living creatures.::
22808::$$$message_0177_0134_0000$$$::"Are you saying that virtue is...a personal value, not something others assign to you?"[lr]::
22809::$$$message_0177_0134_0001$$$::"Huh? No, if we're talking 'value,' then that all comes from the outside.[lr]::
22810::$$$message_0177_0134_0002$$$::It's [font italic=true]why[font italic=false] we try to cultivate our own virtue. Virtue is a parameter we try to raise as high as possible, to hang around people who act like they're better than they really are."::
22811::$$$message_0177_0135_0000$$$::Elevating your inner world influences your presence in the outer world.[lr]::
22812::$$$message_0177_0135_0001$$$::Lonely show-offs are obsessed with being seen as "good people." What a wretched, shameful way to live.[lr]::
22813::$$$message_0177_0135_0002$$$::How self-serving it must be to try to be a good person so that other people won't hate you.[lr]::
22814::$$$message_0177_0135_0003$$$::But...::
22815::$$$message_0177_0136_0000$$$::"...And what's wrong with that? The desire to be acknowledged is actually worth something. [l][say storage=snplg02_anr_0631 name=アンリ]Someone who feels that way can recognize the value of someone else.[lr]::
22816::$$$message_0177_0136_0001$$$::I don't think it's wrong for your values to also benefit you."::
22817::$$$message_0177_0137_0000$$$::That's where the beauty of love is; the desire to enjoy life together.[lr]::
22818::$$$message_0177_0137_0001$$$::She hasn't reached that understanding yet, and it's doubtful she ever will.[lr]::
22819::$$$message_0177_0137_0002$$$::She just doesn't have the knack for it.[lr]::
22820::$$$message_0177_0137_0003$$$::But she's dabbled in everything, making her a jack-of-all-trades.::
22821::$$$message_0177_0138_0000$$$::She's reactionary. And shameless.[lr]::
22822::$$$message_0177_0138_0001$$$::Trying to better herself by single-mindedly taking the long way around.[lr]::
22823::$$$message_0177_0138_0002$$$::She's got herself an inkling that she's in the wrong, but curses herself as nothing special, stuck in a purgatory and clawing her way to something brighter.[lr]::
22824::$$$message_0177_0138_0003$$$::Ahhh... So this is the kind of person I'm helping.::
22825::$$$message_0177_0139_0000$$$::"...Erm.[lr]::
22826::$$$message_0177_0139_0001$$$::Can I interpret your uncharacteristic sermon to mean that you don't have a problem with my direction?"[lr]::
22827::$$$message_0177_0139_0002$$$::"Yeah. Why not champion justice, and all that?[lr]::
22828::$$$message_0177_0139_0003$$$::I bet it's satisfying, swooping in to save people from senseless death."[lr]::
22829::$$$message_0177_0139_0004$$$::That justice stuff is gross and sounds like something out of a comic book or whatever...but it can sound kinda neat, I guess.::
22830::$$$message_0177_0140_0000$$$::"...I'm surprised. I thought that you would despise the concept more than anything."[lr]::
22831::$$$message_0177_0140_0001$$$::"I do. But I like where it leads."[lr]::
22832::$$$message_0177_0140_0002$$$::"Huh?"[lr]::
22833::$$$message_0177_0140_0003$$$::First off, it doesn't change what we have to do.[lr]::
22834::$$$message_0177_0140_0004$$$::We're going to patrol the city at night, kill the other Masters, and kill the monsters. The only difference is that they now have the same priority. And I'm still more than capable of either.::
22835::$$$message_0177_0141_0000$$$::Fuyuki is still full of life.[lr]::
22836::$$$message_0177_0141_0001$$$::The cup won't run dry until my Master is sated.[lr]::
22837::$$$message_0177_0141_0002$$$::While we'll never see victory, we also won't know death, and we'll overcome failure.::
22838::$$$message_0177_0142_0000$$$::"Yeah. Let's do this until you're satisfied, Master.[lr]::
22839::$$$message_0177_0142_0001$$$::Everything's a learning experience. Just enjoy this until you get bored of it."[lr]::
22840::$$$message_0177_0142_0002$$$::The wind whistles a higher note.[lr]::
22841::$$$message_0177_0142_0003$$$::Of course, from up here, so close to the heavens, the city lights may as well be a pipe dream.::
22842::$$$message_0177_0143_0000$$$::The Holy Grail War will continue as long as it takes.[lr]::
22843::$$$message_0177_0143_0001$$$::My murderous pleasure will, too.[lr]::
22844::$$$message_0177_0143_0002$$$::Most likely, we'll lose to another Master tomorrow and revive again.[lr]::
22845::$$$message_0177_0143_0003$$$::I'll stick with her a while longer, until Bazett changes her mind.[lr]::
22846::$$$message_0177_0143_0004$$$::The sky here is distant, deep, and hollow.[lr]::
22847::$$$message_0177_0143_0005$$$::Ultimately, there are only illusions to be gained.::
22848::$$$message_0177_0144_0000$$$::"Let's do this until you're satisfied, Master.[lr]::
22849::$$$message_0177_0144_0001$$$::Everything's a learning experience. Just enjoy this until you get bored of it."[lr]::
22850::$$$message_0177_0144_0002$$$::My Servant breaks eye contact with me.[lr]::
22851::$$$message_0177_0144_0003$$$::I wonder what changed his mind. With that last casual remark, he goes quiet and looks out at the night landscape.::
22852::$$$message_0177_0145_0000$$$::...The Servant Avenger.[lr]::
22853::$$$message_0177_0145_0001$$$::I've heard that on occasion, classes other than the original seven appear during the Holy Grail War. Avenger must be one of them.::
22854::$$$message_0177_0146_0000$$$::A Heroic Spirit of vengeance sounds contradictory, but more than that, his name Aŋra Mainiiu is an enigma.[lr]::
22855::$$$message_0177_0146_0001$$$::There are many cases of heroes later being assigned names that they weren't born with.[lr]::
22856::$$$message_0177_0146_0002$$$::The childhood hero I described is one of them.::
22857::$$$message_0177_0147_0000$$$::But still, Aŋra Mainiiu is just too sinister.[lr]::
22858::$$$message_0177_0147_0001$$$::One day, I'll need to get him to tell me his birth name, not this wicked title.::
22859::$$$message_0177_0148_0000$$$::Dark shadows roam here and there in the city below.[lr]::
22860::$$$message_0177_0148_0001$$$::Even with Kenaz, the Rune of Far-Sight, I can only see as far as the urban Shinto area's borders.[lr]::
22861::$$$message_0177_0148_0002$$$::The Mion River divides Fuyuki in two. I can't find out what's happening across the bridge in Miyama unless I go there myself.[lr]::
22862::$$$message_0177_0148_0003$$$::The black monsters must be lurking out there, too.::
22863::$$$message_0177_0149_0000$$$::...I wonder what magecraft was used to create such familiars.[lr]::
22864::$$$message_0177_0149_0001$$$::I've never seen their type at the Association.[lr]::
22865::$$$message_0177_0149_0002$$$::Cryptically, they do seem to be controlled. They lack intellect, but the way they appear and reappear feels deliberate.::
22866::$$$message_0177_0150_0000$$$::Individually, their combat strength is relatively high. They resemble a hybrid of large canines and feral, oversized primates.[lr]::
22867::$$$message_0177_0150_0001$$$::A human without any combat experience would die instantly against one.[lr]::
22868::$$$message_0177_0150_0002$$$::Someone with at least a decade's training in martial arts or sports might be able to resist for a few seconds or even escape, given favorable conditions.::
22869::$$$message_0177_0151_0000$$$::But they're also numerous.[lr]::
22870::$$$message_0177_0151_0001$$$::And their physical appearance evokes a primal revulsion, with wicked claws and hide as tough as tree bark.[lr]::
22871::$$$message_0177_0151_0002$$$::If multiple of them attacked a person, it would be impossible to survive without firearms.[lr]::
22872::$$$message_0177_0151_0003$$$::And yet...::
22873::$$$message_0177_0152_0000$$$::"[font color=0x000000][block len=9][resetfont]"::
22874::$$$message_0177_0153_0000$$$::Those howls are sickening.[lr]::
22875::$$$message_0177_0153_0001$$$::They're unbearable and grating, nothing like the roar of a majestic beast.[lr]::
22876::$$$message_0177_0153_0002$$$::If insect pests had vocal cords, I bet they would sound like that.::
22877::$$$message_0177_0154_0000$$$::He... Avenger doesn't seem to like the sound.[lr]::
22878::$$$message_0177_0154_0001$$$::In our earlier battle, I saw him exchange blows with the monsters in a businesslike manner.::
22879::$$$message_0177_0155_0000$$$::Of course, there isn't much to say about his skills.[lr]::
22880::$$$message_0177_0155_0001$$$::His claim to be the weakest Servant is correct.[lr]::
22881::$$$message_0177_0155_0002$$$::...It's correct, but should a Heroic Spirit really struggle against that level of fodder? I hope he isn't scamming me.::
22882::$$$message_0177_0156_0000$$$::"It's not a scam. I told you right off the bat that I'm the weakest."[lr]::
22883::$$$message_0177_0156_0001$$$::"...Wait. You can read my mind?"[lr]::
22884::$$$message_0177_0156_0002$$$::"Nope. I was just responding to that ugly look you gave me. It'd be pretty funny if I could read minds, though. I bet you're a mess both inside and out."::
22885::$$$message_0177_0157_0000$$$::My Servant laughs shamelessly.[lr]::
22886::$$$message_0177_0157_0001$$$::He's so boorish and not suited to me at all. Plus he's weak. [l]And all talk. [l]I'll have to do the heavy lifting in our rematch with Saber.::
22887::$$$message_0177_0158_0000$$$::...Still, it isn't all bad.[lr]::
22888::$$$message_0177_0158_0001$$$::This Servant is singularly talented at not dying.[lr]::
22889::$$$message_0177_0158_0002$$$::He'll revive on death, so he can't be permanently killed, but his mental fortitude makes him good in a defensive fight.::
22890::$$$message_0177_0159_0000$$$::In the brawl earlier, for example...[lr]::
22891::$$$message_0177_0159_0001$$$::I was eliminating the enemies enveloping me at a rate of one per second.[lr]::
22892::$$$message_0177_0159_0002$$$::He, on the other hand, held out against the enemies around him until I could come over to back him up.[lr]::
22893::$$$message_0177_0159_0003$$$::His fighting style is about neither winning nor losing.[lr]::
22894::$$$message_0177_0159_0004$$$::I hate to admit it, but our tactics are exceedingly compatible.::
22895::$$$message_0177_0160_0000$$$::The wind picks up again.[lr]::
22896::$$$message_0177_0160_0001$$$::I see my Servant's hair wafting in the corner of my eye.[lr]::
22897::$$$message_0177_0160_0002$$$::"...Huh?"[lr]::
22898::$$$message_0177_0160_0003$$$::The primitive shaman accepts the wind wafting up from the wasteland.[lr]::
22899::$$$message_0177_0160_0004$$$::I see a vision of him taking in nature for what it is, simply choosing to live and die with it.::
22900::$$$message_0177_0161_0000$$$::"...Avenger, just now..."[lr]::
22901::$$$message_0177_0161_0001$$$::"Let's get going. You know where they're grouped up, right? You'll feel better once we find and take 'em out."[lr]::
22902::$$$message_0177_0161_0002$$$::...I must have imagined it.[lr]::
22903::$$$message_0177_0161_0003$$$::Avenger was looking for a gathering of the monsters.::
22904::$$$message_0177_0162_0000$$$::"Yeah, no point overthinking it.[lr]::
22905::$$$message_0177_0162_0001$$$::Hehe, you're a sly one, Master. In the end, you're still asking me to kill all the enemies I see."[lr]::
22906::$$$message_0177_0162_0002$$$::Twirling his wicked knives, Avenger's lips curl into a genuine smile of delight.[lr]::
22907::$$$message_0177_0162_0003$$$::He just needs to kill.[lr]::
22908::$$$message_0177_0162_0004$$$::It doesn't matter if they're humans or animals.[lr]::
22909::$$$message_0177_0162_0005$$$::They're all beasts in the end.::
22910::$$$message_0177_0163_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
22911::$$$message_0177_0163_0001$$$::I glare at my Servant.[lr]::
22912::$$$message_0177_0163_0002$$$::"Ugh. Sorry, sorry. I won't kill any people. I'll only go after the Masters or monsters, so stop giving me that look... Argh, what a drag. My Master is so small-minded, unlike her chest."::
22913::$$$message_0177_0164_0000$$$::He disappears into the building, making his crude jokes all the while.[lr]::
22914::$$$message_0177_0164_0001$$$::"...He's awful. He's always like that, no matter what he says."[lr]::
22915::$$$message_0177_0164_0002$$$::I sigh and leave the rooftop.[lr]::
22916::$$$message_0177_0164_0003$$$::Above me, the moon is ominous. Below me, the city resembles the ocean abyss.[lr]::
22917::$$$message_0177_0164_0004$$$::I feel loathing and suspicion for the Servant fighting with me.[lr]::
22918::$$$message_0177_0164_0005$$$::The variables just keep piling up in this Holy Grail War.[lr]::
22919::$$$message_0177_0164_0006$$$::...Regardless, that Servant feels slightly friendlier than yesterday.::
22920::$$$message_0177_0165_0000$$$::   He was gazing out at the city.[lr]::
22921::$$$message_0177_0165_0001$$$::When I saw his indifferent expression, I couldn't help but think[lr]::
22922::$$$message_0177_0165_0002$$$::that he was incorrigibly evil.[lr]::
22923::$$$message_0177_0165_0003$$$::And yet, contradictorily...[lr]::
22924::$$$message_0177_0165_0004$$$::I also felt that he loved the world and the people in it.::
922591::$$$message_9177_0071_0000$$$::Aŋra Mainiiu is the name of one of the greatest devils of ancient Persia.[r]::

